<!-- ===================== 3. MONTHLY QUOTA ===================== -->
<section class="view" id="quota">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="callout" style="margin-bottom:24px;"><strong>Interface model.</strong> Clip counters and monthly quota progress are not connected to a content database yet.</div>
    <span class="eyebrow">The deal</span>
    <h2 class="display">10 clips a month, minimum.<br/>No upper cap.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Volume plus variety is what moves the algorithm. The quota is 10 distinct use cases per month — one of each. Post more if you want. Every extra clip is another shot at viral kickers, Spark bonuses, and Wildcard draws.</p>

    <div class="card" style="background:var(--gold-soft);border-color:transparent;margin-bottom:48px;">
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;align-items:center;">
        <div>
          <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;margin-bottom:8px;">The minimum</div>
          <div style="font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-2.5px;line-height:1;">10<span style="font-size:24px;font-weight:500;color:var(--mute);"> clips/mo</span></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;margin-bottom:8px;">The ceiling</div>
          <div style="font-size:64px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-2.5px;line-height:1;">∞</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;margin-bottom:8px;">Reset</div>
          <div style="font-size:42px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.5px;line-height:1;">1st of month</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--mute);margin-top:6px;">AWST · zero rollovers</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>The 10 use cases</h3>
    <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--mute);margin-bottom:24px;">One clip in each category covers the monthly quota. Mix formats — at least 3 vertical TikTok-native, 2 IG Reels, the rest your call.</p>

    <div class="uc-grid">
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">01 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Pre-session</span>
        <h3>Warming up</h3>
        <p>Dynamic warm-up, foam roll, band work, hip openers. Cracking the sachet as the last beat before the heavy stuff starts.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 15–30s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical, sound on</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">02 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Pre-session</span>
        <h3>Stretching &amp; mobility</h3>
        <p>Long-format. Run through your mobility routine. We use the best for tutorial-style carousels and longer ads. Audio matters.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 30–60s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical or carousel</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">03 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">In-session</span>
        <h3>Mid-session action</h3>
        <p>The grit shot. Mid-set, mid-round, mid-rep. Sweat visible, breathing audible. The Reactor-tier clips usually live here.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 10–20s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical, single take</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">04 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">In-session</span>
        <h3>Consuming HEX</h3>
        <p>The sachet crack. Pour into bottle or shaker. No talking — clean audio of the rip and the pour. The signature HEX moment.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 5–10s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical, clean backdrop</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">05 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Post-session</span>
        <h3>Cooldown</h3>
        <p>Finish line, last rep done, gear off. The exhale moment. Audience reads this as honest — it's the trust beat.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 15–30s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">06 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Recovery</span>
        <h3>Recovery &amp; next-day</h3>
        <p>Day-after content. Soreness check, recovery routine, foam roll, ice bath, sauna, walk. HEX in hand as the throughline.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 20–40s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical or photo carousel</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">07 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Lifestyle</span>
        <h3>Morning ritual</h3>
        <p>First HEX of the day. Alarm, kettle, sachet, out the door. Wins on relatability — audiences see their morning in your morning.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 15–25s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">08 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Lifestyle</span>
        <h3>Pre-event ritual</h3>
        <p>Pre-race, pre-fight, pre-set. The walk-out moment. Sachet crack as the last grounding beat before show-time.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 10–30s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical, dramatic</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">09 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Lifestyle</span>
        <h3>Travel / on-the-road</h3>
        <p>FIFO swing-back, festival lineup, work trip, surf trip. HEX out of a backpack. Sachet format is the whole edge here.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 15–30s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Vertical</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="uc-card">
        <div class="uc-num">10 / 10</div>
        <span class="uc-pill">Story</span>
        <h3>Side-by-side · before / after</h3>
        <p>Split-screen, energy check at 3pm, "what HEX is actually doing." The honest receipt. Best for retention &amp; conversion.</p>
        <div class="uc-meta"><span><strong>Duration</strong> 20–45s</span><span><strong>Format</strong> Split-screen, captioned</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <h3>The math on extra clips.</h3>
      <p>Quota is 10. The top Reactors usually file 30–50 clips a month. Every extra clip is one more shot at a viral kicker ($250–$25k), one more chance to win the Spark bonus ($500–$5k), and one more entry into the Wildcard draws. The 11th clip costs you nothing and could be the one that hits 5M views.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

